 "notes": "Boundary of the red 90% CL excluded region in Fig. 4 (main panel, |g_gamma/g_gamma^KSVZ| vs m_a), digitised from the e-print raster Fig4_pace_exclusion_plot.jpg with pixel-level tick calibration (x: 10.0-11.5 ueV linear, y: 10^0-10^4 log). Main band (10.16-11.37 ueV, ~7-11x KSVZ from the 9KSVZ runs) binned as per-bin medians of the per-column lower envelope; the narrow KSVZ-run notch at 10.7126-10.7186 ueV (down to ~1.13x KSVZ) is sampled explicitly. Ratio converted to g_agamma using the paper's own convention: g_KSVZ = 0.97*alpha_em/(pi*f_a) with f_a*m_a = (78 MeV)^2 [Eq. (1), refs 23,25], giving g_KSVZ ~ 3.96e-15 GeV^-1 at 10.7 ueV. Paper assumes rho_a = 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (matches canonical density, no rescaling) and a virialized axion line shape. Small gaps (bluetooth interference near 2.48 GHz, TE mode crossings) are interpolated over by the binning.",
